# Line-ending policy, made explicit.
#
# Without this file, how a line ending gets stored depends on each
# machine's `core.autocrlf` setting rather than on anything in the repo.
# That is why `git status` was reporting modifications to files nobody had
# edited -- adp.py, keepers.py, scoring.py, team_codes.py and friends --
# and why every commit risked carrying a whole-file rewrite that buries
# the three real changed lines inside it.
#
# `text=auto` tells git to normalize to LF in the repository and check out
# whatever the platform expects. Windows working copies stay CRLF, the
# stored history stays LF, and the decision now lives in the repo instead
# of in a global setting on one laptop.
* text=auto

# Explicitly text, so a stray setting can never mangle them.
*.py    text
*.md    text
*.json  text
*.csv   text
*.ipynb text

# Binary. Line-ending translation on a zip container (which is what an
# .xlsx is) corrupts the file, and diffing one produces noise rather than
# information.
*.xlsx  binary
*.xls   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
